now.\n\nFiles to write:\n1. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/BrazilianSoccerMcp.csproj (update)\n2. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/DataPaths.cs\n3. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/CsvReader.cs\n4. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs\n5. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/DataLoader.cs\n6. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Models/MatchRecord.cs\n7. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Models/PlayerRecord.cs\n8. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Models/Competition.cs (enum)\n9. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Services/MatchService.cs\n10. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Services/TeamService.cs\n11. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Services/PlayerService.cs\n12. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Services/CompetitionService.cs\n13. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Services/StatisticsService.cs\n14. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Services/SoccerDataStore.cs (aggregate facade)\n15. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Mcp/McpServer.cs\n16. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Mcp/JsonRpc.cs\n17. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Mcp/Tools.cs (tool definitions & dispatcher)\n18. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Mcp/ToolRegistry.cs\n19. src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Program.cs (update to run MCP server)\n20. tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/MatchQueryTests.cs\n21. tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/TeamQueryTests.cs\n22. tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/PlayerQueryTests.cs\n23. tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/CompetitionQueryTests.cs\n24. tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/StatisticsQueryTests.cs\n25. tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/McpServerTests.cs\n26. tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/GlobalUsings.cs (maybe already there)\n\nLet me delete UnitTest1.cs default.\n\nLet me start writing. First, the models.\n\nLet me think about MatchRecord unified model. Each match from different files has different fields. I'll create one MatchRecord with optional fields:\n\n```\npublic sealed record MatchRecord(\n    string Competition,       // \"Brasileirao\", \"CopaDoBrasil\", \"Libertadores\", \"BR-Football\", \"HistoricoBrasileirao\"\n    DateTime Date,\n    string Home,              // normalized\n    string Away,              // normalized\n    string HomeRaw,\n    string AwayRaw,\n    int HomeGoal,\n    int AwayGoal,\n    int? Season,\n    string? Round,\n    string? Stage,\n    string? HomeState,\n    string? AwayState,\n    string? Arena,\n    string? Tournament     // for BR-Football\n);\n```\n\nPlayerRecord:\n```\npublic sealed record PlayerRecord(\n    int Id, string Name, int Age, string Nationality, int Overall, int Potential,\n    string Club, string Position, int? JerseyNumber, string? PreferredFoot\n);\n```\n\nCSV reader: I'll write a simple RFC4180-ish parser that handles quoted fields with escaped quotes. Returns List<string[]> and header.\n\nLet me write the CSV reader:\n\n```csharp\npublic static class CsvReader\n{\n    public static List<string[]> Read(TextReader reader, bool hasHeader);\n}\n```\n\nActually let me write a method that takes a path and returns (header, rows).\n\nLet me handle encoding (UTF-8). File.OpenRead with UTF8 encoding.\n\nLet me now write the team name normalizer. The data has:\n- \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"Palmeiras\"\n- \"Sport-PE\" → \"Sport\"\n- \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → \"Boavista\" (complex!)\n- \"América - MG\" → \"America\"\n- \"Athletico-PR\" → \"Athletico\"\n- \"Nacional (URU)\" → keep \"Nacional\" ( Uruguay disambig)\n- \"Barcelona-EQU\"\n- \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → \"Corinthians\"\n\nHmm normalization is tricky. Let me make a normalization that:\n1. Strip trailing \"- XX\" state suffix where XX is 2-letter state code\n2. Strip \"(...)\" parenthetical\n3. Strip \" (antigo ...)\" \n4. Map full official names to common short names via a dictionary\n\nLet me build a dictionary of common aliases for known teams, and a fallback normalizer that strips suffixes/parentheses. Let me create a KnownAliases dictionary with maybe 40 teams.\n\nActually let me keep it simpler: a function NormalizeTeamName that:\n- Removes content in parentheses\n- Removes trailing \" - XX\" or \"-XX\" where XX is a 2-letter uppercase code\n- Removes accent (normalize to ASCII? No, keep accents but strip suffix)\n- Trims\n- Applies a KnownAliases dictionary\n\nLet me include known aliases for common Brazilian teams. The dataset has many teams; I'll include main ones and rely on the suffix stripper for the rest.\n\nFor matching, store both normalized and raw. When searching by team name, normalize the query too and compare against normalized home/away. But also allow substring match on raw.\n\nLet me also have a ContainsTeamName function for matching a query team against a match's normalized home/away (with the alias map applied both ways).\n\nLet me write the code now. I'll be efficient.\n\nLet me start writing files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eeca5b23d0017scHWCI8TMeX0y","sessionID":"ses_1135b46adffe7APFrgclWh2WTn","messageID":"msg_eeca56998001P7iB5A3aHLfztt"}}
