",\n [\"Atlético Clube Goianiense\"] = \"Atletico-GO\",\n [\"Atlético Goianiense\"] = \"Atletico-GO\",\n+[\"Atletico-GO\"] = \"Atletico-GO\",\n [\"Atlético Mineiro\"] = \"Atletico-MG\",\n+[\"Atletico-MG\"] = \"Atletico-MG\",\n+[\"Atlético Mineiro - MG\"] = \"Atletico-MG\",\n [\"America Futebol Clube MG\"] = \"America-MG\",\n [\"América Futebol Clube\"] = \"America-MG\",\n [\"América Mineiro\"] = \"America-MG\",\n [\"América - MG\"] = \"America-MG\",\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-2vdvakbf/retort-a07630997387/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-2vdvakbf/retort-a07630997387/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-2vdvakbf/retort-a07630997387/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-2vdvakbf/retort-a07630997387/src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs\n@@ -40,11 +40,15 @@\n [\"Botafogo R.J.\"] = \"Botafogo\",\n [\"Botafogo-RJ\"] = \"Botafogo\",\n [\"Club Athletico Paranaense\"] = \"Athletico-PR\",\n [\"Athletico Paranaense\"] = \"Athletico-PR\",\n+[\"Athletico-PR\"] = \"Athletico-PR\",\n [\"Atlético Clube Goianiense\"] = \"Atletico-GO\",\n [\"Atlético Goianiense\"] = \"Atletico-GO\",\n+[\"Atletico-GO\"] = \"Atletico-GO\",\n [\"Atlético Mineiro\"] = \"Atletico-MG\",\n+[\"Atletico-MG\"] = \"Atletico-MG\",\n+[\"Atlético Mineiro - MG\"] = \"Atletico-MG\",\n [\"America Futebol Clube MG\"] = \"America-MG\",\n [\"América Futebol Clube\"] = \"America-MG\",\n [\"América Mineiro\"] = \"America-MG\",\n [\"América - MG\"] = \"America-MG\",\n","additions":4,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/Data/TeamNameNormalizer.cs","time":{"start":1782087123474,"end":1782087123478}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now write the BDD/GWT structured tests. The spec asks for BDD GWT (Given/When/Then) structured tests. I'll write xUnit tests organized with GWT comments/regions. I'll create test classes:\n- MatchQueryTests\n- TeamQueryTests\n- PlayerQueryTests\n- CompetitionQueryTests\n- StatisticsQueryTests\n- NormalizationTests\n- McpServerTests\n\nI want to make sure tests actually pass against real data. Let me write tests that use the actual loaded data. But tests need data to be present. Since the repo has data/kaggle, the DataPaths will find it by walking up from bin dir. Good.\n\nLet me be careful about test expectations. I'll use assertions that are robust given the real data:\n- MatchQueryTests: search Flamengo matches in Brasileirao -> not empty; head_to_head Flamengo vs Fluminense -> > 0 matches and tallies sum to total; last_match_between returns a match with both teams involved.\n- TeamQueryTests: Corinthians home record in 2022 -> played>0, wins+draws+losses=played.\n- PlayerQueryTests: search Brazilian players top -> count>0 and sorted by overall desc; Neymar exists; brazilian_players_by_club -> non-empty.\n- CompetitionQueryTests: get_standings 2019 -> rows>0, position 1 is champion (Flamengo in 2019). Champion for 2019 == Flamengo.\n- StatisticsQueryTests: average_goals > 0; outcome_rates sum ~100; biggest_wins sorted by margin desc.\n- NormalizationTests: normalize \"Palmeiras-SP\" == \"Palmeiras\"; \"Sport-PE\" == \"Sport\"; \"Corinthians\" full name == \"Corinthians\"; \"América - MG\" == \"America-MG\"; matches.\n- McpServerTests: send initialize, tools/list, tools/call head_to_head via in-memory reader/writer, assert responses parse.\n\nLet me check that 2019 champion is Flamengo in the modern Brasileirao file (seasons 2012-2023). The data file has 2012-2023. 2019 Brasileirao champion was Flamengo. Good. But our standings computed from match results should yield Flamengo at top. Let me verify with a quick check after writing. Actually I should test empirically. Let me write a quick console check first by running the loader. Let me write a quick test program... actually let me just write the tests and run them, then adjust assertions.\n\nFor 2019 standings - let me make the assertion flexible: champion team's normalized name contains \"Flamengo\". Actually safer: just check rows non-empty and position 1 has highest points.\n\nLet me write tests now.\n\nFor the normalizer, \"Palmeiras-SP\" — my StripSuffix: dashIndex finds the \"-\", tail=\"SP\", state code SP -> strip -> \"Palmeiras\". Good. But wait, there's an alias entry \"Portuguesa-SP\" => \"Portuguesa\" and Aliased checks the trimmed value first. \"Palmeiras-SP\" is not a direct alias key. Then StripParentheses no-op. Aliased again no. Then StripSuffix -> \"Palmeiras\". Aliased(\"Palmeiras\")? Not in dict. Returns \"Palmeiras\". Good.\n\n\"Sport-PE\" -> not alias, strip -> \"Sport\". Good. But there's alias \"Sport Recife\" => \"Sport\" and \"Sport Club do Recife\" => \"Sport\". \"Sport-PE\" raw -> \"Sport\". Good.\n\n\"Corinthians\" -> no alias, no parens, no suffix. Returns \"Corinthians\". Good. Full name \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" is an alias -> \"Corinthians\". Good.\n\n\"América - MG\" -> not alias, strip parens no, StripSuffix: collapsed \"América - MG\", dashIndex = lastIndexOf('-') = position of \"-\". tail after = \" MG\" trimmed \"MG\". firstToken = \"MG\". MG is state code -> return \"América\". Hmm wait, we want \"America-MG\" not \"América\". My alias has \"América - MG\" => \"America-MG\". But the alias check happens BEFORE strip suffix. So \"América - MG\" matches alias directly -> \"America-MG\". Good.\n\nBut \"América Mineiro\" -> alias -> \"America-MG\". Good.\n\nLet me check \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\". Direct alias? Not exact. StripParentheses -> \"Boavista Sport Club\" (the (antigo...) removed, and \" - RJ\" remains? Wait the string is \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\". StripParentheses removes the parenthetical leaving \"Boavista Sport Club  - RJ\" -> collapse -> \"Boavista Sport Club - RJ\". Aliased? no. StripSuffix: dashIndex at \"-\", tail \"RJ\" -> strip -> \"Boavista Sport Club\". Aliased? The key \"Boavista Sport Club\" exists -> \"Boavista\". \n\nNow the historic file uses \"Guarani\", \"Vasco\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Grêmio\". Normalize \"Grêmio\" -> alias -> \"Gremio\". \"Athletico-PR\" -> alias direct \"Athletico-PR\"? Yes \"Athletico-PR\" is not a direct key but \"Athletico Paranaense\" is. \"Athletico-PR\" -> strip suffix -> \"Athletico\". Hmm we want \"Athletico-PR\" canonical. Actually there's no key \"Athletico-PR\". After strip suffix it becomes \"Athletico\". That may conflict with \"Atletico-MG\" normalization? \"Atletico-MG\" -> no direct alias -> strip suffix -> \"Atletico\". That would conflate Athletico-PR and Atletico-MG into \"Atletico\". That's bad for head-to-head.\n\nLet me add direct aliases: \"Athletico-PR\" => \"Athletico-PR\", \"Atletico-MG\" => \"Atletico-MG\", \"Atletico-GO\" => \"Atletico-GO\". Actually I have alias keys \"Atlético Mineiro\" => \"Atletico-MG\" etc. But raw \"Atletico-MG\" isn't a key. Let me add them. Actually for matching it might be okay because they'd both become \"Atletico\" and queries for \"Atletico-MG\" would also strip to \"Atletico\" and match both. Bad.\n\nLet me add direct aliases for the dash-suffixed canonical forms so StripSuffix isn't applied. Add:\n\"Athletico-PR\" => \"Athletico-PR\"\n\"Atletico-MG\" => \"Atletico-MG\"\n\"Atletico-GO\" => \"Atletico-GO\"\n\"America-MG\" => \"America-MG\" (already)\n\"America-RJ\" => \"America-RJ\" (already)\n\"America-SP\" => \"America-SP\" (already)\n\"Vasco\" => \"Vasco\" (already via \"Vasco da Gama\")\n\"Vasco-RJ\" => \"Vasco\"\n\nActually simpler: in Aliased check, also check after strip-suffix? The order is direct, then stripParens+alias, then stripSuffix+alias. For \"Atletico-MG\", direct alias fails, stripParens no-op alias fails, stripSuffix -> \"Atletico\" alias fails -> returns \"Atletico\". So both Atletico-MG and Athletico-PR -> \"Atletico\". Bad.\n\nLet me add direct alias keys for all the \"X-UF\" canonical forms of major teams so they're preserved. I'll add:\n\"Atletico-MG\", \"Athletico-PR\", \"Atletico-GO\", \"Vasco-RJ\", \"Gremio-RS\", \"Internacional-RS\", \"Bahia-BA\", \"Vitoria-BA\", \"Ceara-CE\", \"CriciUma-SC\", \"Goias-GO\", \"Cuiaba-MT\"\n\nBut the modern Brasileirao file stores teams with suffix already (\"Palmeiras-SP\"). For those we WANT to strip to base name \"Palmeiras\". The issue is only teams where the dash form IS the canonical disambiguator (Atletico-MG vs Atletico-GO vs Athletico-PR).\n\nLet me add direct aliases for the ambiguous Atletico/America teams:\n\"Athletico-PR\" => \"Athletico-PR\"\n\"Atletico-MG\" => \"Atletico-MG\"  \n\"Atletico-GO\" => \"Atletico-GO\"\n\nAnd keep the others stripping. That solves the main conflict.\n\nAlso \"America-MG\", \"America-RJ\", \"America-SP\" already aliased.\n\nLet me add those three. Also \"Botafogo-RJ\" => \"Botafogo\" already exists, \"Botafogo-SP\" => \"Botafogo-SP\" exists. Good.\n\nLet me update the normalizer.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecab7cf9001qXdH2I0rWQZq0Q","sessionID":"ses_1135b46adffe7APFrgclWh2WTn","messageID":"msg_eecab24b0001wFDJQrJr92PA3g"}}
