{"type":"text","timestamp":1782087270912,"sessionID":"ses_1135b46adffe7APFrgclWh2WTn","part":{"id":"prt_eecadac20001pCFMQqPbOTNclX","messageID":"msg_eecada8df001ZgJhIkZkW3b3bv","sessionID":"ses_1135b46adffe7APFrgclWh2WTn","type":"text","text":"Done. The Brazilian Soccer MCP server is implemented in C# (.NET 10) and everything builds and tests pass (31/31).\n\n## What was built\n\n**Solution**: `BrazilianSoccerMcp.slnx` with two projects:\n- `src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/` — console app + stdio MCP server\n- `tests/BrazilianSoccerMcp.Tests/` — xUnit BDD/GWT tests\n\n**Source layout** (`src/BrazilianSoccerMcp/`):\n- `Data/` — `DataPaths`, `CsvReader` (RFC4180-ish, offline/no deps), `DateParser` (3 formats), `TeamNameNormalizer` (suffix/parenthetical stripping + alias map), `DataLoader` (loads all 6 CSVs into unified models)\n- `Models/` — `MatchRecord`, `PlayerRecord`, `Competition` enum\n- `Services/` — `SoccerDataStore`, `MatchService`, `TeamService`, `PlayerService`, `CompetitionService` (computed standings), `StatisticsService`, `ResponseFormatter`\n- `Mcp/` — `McpServer` (newline-delimited JSON-RPC over stdio: `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, `ping`, `tools/list`, `tools/call`) and `ToolRegistry` (14 tools covering all 5 spec categories)\n- `Program.cs` — wires store→registry→server\n\n**Tools exposed**: `search_matches`, `head_to_head`, `last_match_between`, `get_team_stats`, `compare_teams`, `search_players`, `top_brazilian_players`, `brazilian_players_by_club`, `get_standings`, `get_champion`, `get_average_goals`, `get_outcome_rates`, `get_biggest_wins`, `best_away_record`.\n\n**Verification**:\n- `dotnet build BrazilianSoccerMcp.slnx` → 0 warnings, 0 errors\n- `dotnet test` → 31 passed, 0 failed\n- Live stdio smoke test correctly returned `2019 Brasileirao Champion: Flamengo (90 pts)` and the top-3 Brazilian players (Neymar 92, Casemiro 88, Coutinho 88)\n\nEvery code file opens with a context-block comment describing its purpose, as requested by the repo conventions. No commits were made.\n\nRun the server: `dotnet run --project src/BrazilianSoccerMcp` and feed JSON-RPC lines on stdin.","time":{"start":1782087265312,"end":1782087270909}}}
